// Curated overrides of JMdict's readings, in inline notation: each is added as
// a row of JMdict and pins its reading as the default. JMdict's frequency tags
// belong to a written form, so across entries they cannot tell two readings
// apart; and a form that drops its okurigana usually meets it in running text,
// where the font cannot see it. A kanji run with no reading is left bare when
// alone in a run, though one reading dominates: the reading depends on the word
// around it, which a font cannot see past the run. Users' pins override these.
// Add entries with `pnpm dict:override`.
[
  // 出来る, 出来た: しゅったい is rare.
  "出[で]来[き]",
  // なにびと is literary.
  "何[なん]人[にん]",
  // いつ is mostly written in kana.
  "何[なん]時[じ]",
  // The date; みそか is the last day of a month.
  "三[さん]十[じゅう]日[にち]",
  // Nearly always written 外付け.
  "外[そと]付[づ]",
  // 支払い, 支払う.
  "支[し]払[はら]",
  // Alone, 字 is a character; あざ is a village section and ranks higher. A run
  // of kanji never includes the kana before it, so ローマ字 reaches the font as 字.
  "字[じ]",
  // 明朝体 is read みんちょう; みょうちょう is the dynasty's old reading.
  "明[みん]朝[ちょう]",
  // 月 is つき in a poem and がつ in a date.
  "月",
  "日",
  "年",
  // 白浪 is しらなみ (white waves, a thief; 白浪物); はくろう is the rare literary reading.
  // reported by 中院凛音 b42bf3c9-ffbd-4d24-bb86-c46dde64acd6
  "白[しら]浪[なみ]",
  // The shogun is read みなもとのよりとも, with の after the clan name 源.
  // reported by anonymous 8c2df88c-4638-4d31-b9c8-905e90635e98
  "源[みなもとの]頼[より]朝[とも]",
  // Alone, 凪 is なぎ (a calm; also a given name); JMdict has only な, from 凪ぐ.
  "凪[なぎ]"
]
